      "text": "Given that the least common multiple (LCM) of two integers is 36 and their greatest common divisor (GCD) is 6, we can use the relationship between LCM and GCD to find the two integers.\n\nThe product of two numbers is the product of their LCM and GCD:\n\\[ \\text{Product} = \\text{LCM} \\times \\text{GCD} \\]\n\nSubstitute the given values:\n\\[ \\text{Product} = 36 \\times 6 \\]\n\nCalculate the product:\n\\[ 36 \\times 6 = 216 \\]\n\nThus, the product of the two numbers is \\boxed{216}.",
