    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Given that the least common multiple (LCM) of two numbers is 36 and their greatest common divisor (GCD) is 6, we can use the relationship between LCM and GCD for two numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\), which is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) \\times \\text{GCD}(a, b) = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nHere, we are given:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM}(a, b) = 36 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\text{GCD}(a, b) = 6\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these values into the relationship, we get:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = a \\times b\n\\]\n\nCalculating the product on the left-hand side:\n\\[\n36 \\times 6 = 216\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of the two numbers \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{216}\n\\]",
